###### 3.3 Bishops *Change of Variables* Notation 

Bishop & Bishop (2024, p. 42) use a slightly different notation. They swap the roles of the variables, so that the following holds:

$x = g(y)$
$y = g^{-1}(x)$
$x = g(g^{-1}(x)),$
$y = g^{-1}(g(y)),$
$\tilde f(y) = f(g(y)).$

We stick with the *first* notation.
"

